1
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:05,520
What do you wanna eat, Teng?

2
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:06,120
I'm good with anything.

3
00:00:06,120 --> 00:00:06,960
Take a look.

4
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:08,420
(Chef's checking his options)
Anything you make.

5
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:17,120
I'll make grilled beef
with water celery.

6
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:17,960
And stir-fry some glass noodles.

7
00:00:17,960 --> 00:00:18,863
(Bing's menu: Grilled beef with celery,)
Sounds great.

8
00:00:18,863 --> 00:00:19,460
(stir-fried glass noodles)
Sounds great.

9
00:00:21,040 --> 00:00:22,320
Eggplant.

10
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:23,640
Craving it?

11
00:00:23,720 --> 00:00:24,680
Yours?

12
00:00:24,680 --> 00:00:26,320
Your eggplant?

13
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,800
(Huang Jingyu's stuffed eggplant)
Meat stuffed in eggplant.

14
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:31,100
(Eggplant memories)

15
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:32,000
Natural?

16
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:32,710
Very healthy.

17
00:00:34,120 --> 00:00:35,600
Don't, Jingyu.

18
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:35,960
Craving it?

19
00:00:35,960 --> 00:00:37,800
(Not feeling diet food)
No, calm down.

20
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:39,760
No one wants to eat healthy today?

21
00:00:39,840 --> 00:00:41,120
I want that eggplant sauce.

22
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:42,360
(He just doesn't like my eggplant)
Eggplant sauce.

23
00:00:42,440 --> 00:00:43,400
Eggplant and potato sauce.

24
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:44,100
Let's do it.

25
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:44,900
(Bing's menu: eggplant and potato sauce)

26
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:47,040
Bing, how many potatoes?

27
00:00:47,120 --> 00:00:47,760
Two's enough.

28
00:00:47,760 --> 00:00:48,320
These are huge.

29
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:49,000
Peel them?

30
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:49,540
Yeah. Here.

31
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:50,900
(Hired for kitchen duty)

32
00:00:51,080 --> 00:00:52,200
I can wash stuff too.

33
00:00:52,280 --> 00:00:54,040
There's already a line for washing.

34
00:00:54,040 --> 00:00:54,560
No spot for me?

35
00:00:54,560 --> 00:00:55,540
Three people beat you to it.

36
00:00:55,540 --> 00:00:56,980
(Kitchen jobs are in high demand)

37
00:00:58,560 --> 00:00:59,720
I can...

38
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:00,800
I can peel them.

39
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:01,200
I'll peel them.

40
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:01,800
Let us do it.

41
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:03,200
We'll peel them.

42
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:04,200
(Just loves helping)
This job...

43
00:01:04,280 --> 00:01:05,080
Look at them fighting over it.

44
00:01:05,080 --> 00:01:06,120
Then what are you guys doing?

45
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:06,600
Watching.

46
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:07,880
(Speaking from experience)
We watch.

47
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:09,720
Usually at this point,

48
00:01:09,720 --> 00:01:12,030
if there's work, grab it. If not, watch.

49
00:01:15,960 --> 00:01:18,520
You really had to stick
a chopstick in it?

50
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:19,720
(Pro move)
You can tell he does this all the time.

51
00:01:19,720 --> 00:01:20,960
Gotta know a few life hacks.

52
00:01:20,960 --> 00:01:21,320
Of course.

53
00:01:21,320 --> 00:01:22,280
Look at you.

54
00:01:22,280 --> 00:01:23,560
I tried to play it so cool,

55
00:01:23,560 --> 00:01:24,280
and you still noticed.

56
00:01:27,180 --> 00:01:28,860
(Trying to stay calm)

57
00:01:28,860 --> 00:01:30,100
(No one saw that, right?)

58
00:01:31,540 --> 00:01:33,980
(Just wash it and it's fine)

59
00:01:36,080 --> 00:01:37,560
Bing, what else can I do?

60
00:01:37,560 --> 00:01:38,560
Churan, here.

61
00:01:38,560 --> 00:01:41,120
Mince some garlic.

62
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:41,790
Okay.

63
00:01:41,790 --> 00:01:43,240
(Successfully hired)

64
00:01:43,240 --> 00:01:44,800
I'll wash my hands.

65
00:01:44,880 --> 00:01:46,520
I found myself a job too.

66
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:48,000
Wash your hands and wait for dinner.

67
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:52,400
That's honestly the most important step.

68
00:01:52,480 --> 00:01:53,800
I haven't even had a snack.

69
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:54,950
I've held out this whole time.

70
00:01:57,260 --> 00:01:57,932
(Eggplant and potato sauce)

71
00:01:57,932 --> 00:01:58,580
(1. Render the pork belly)

72
00:01:58,580 --> 00:01:59,934
(2. Saute scallions and ginger)

73
00:01:59,934 --> 00:02:01,900
(3. Add potatoes and eggplant,
then stir-fry)

74
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,370
Such a familiar sight.

75
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:12,660
(All eyes are on this pot again)

76
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:16,280
Feels like this year,

77
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:19,300
everything's come full circle.

78
00:02:19,420 --> 00:02:26,700
(Every year starts with this first bite)

79
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:33,020
(4. Add soybean paste
and stir-fry until fragrant)

80
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:37,840
Smells so good.

81
00:02:38,040 --> 00:02:38,600
So good.

82
00:02:38,660 --> 00:02:40,140
(Speaking from the heart)

83
00:02:50,720 --> 00:02:51,630
What's its name?

84
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:53,920
It's joining us this season

85
00:02:53,920 --> 00:02:55,000
on Natural High Season 4

86
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:55,520
as our new buddy.

87
00:02:55,520 --> 00:02:56,550
It'll be with us along the way.

88
00:02:56,960 --> 00:02:58,320
It doesn't have a name yet.

89
00:02:58,320 --> 00:02:59,680
So we'll leave
that important job to you.

90
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:02,600
Baa-Baa. Let's call it Baa-Baa.

91
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:03,960
You're just saying

92
00:03:04,040 --> 00:03:04,960
whatever comes to mind.

93
00:03:04,960 --> 00:03:05,730
Does it look like a sheep?

94
00:03:07,180 --> 00:03:08,500
Baa-Baa.

95
00:03:08,720 --> 00:03:10,000
Puppy.

96
00:03:10,080 --> 00:03:10,600
Here.

97
00:03:10,680 --> 00:03:12,080
Baa-Baa. How's that?

98
00:03:13,240 --> 00:03:13,940
Baa-Baa.

99
00:03:15,960 --> 00:03:17,000
It reacted.

100
00:03:17,080 --> 00:03:18,360
Baa-Baa.

101
00:03:20,640 --> 00:03:21,960
It's thirsty now. Hold on.

102
00:03:21,960 --> 00:03:22,430
Baa-Baa.

103
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:25,120
Let's just call it Baa-Baa.

104
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:27,240
Hungry?

105
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:28,080
Starving.

106
00:03:28,160 --> 00:03:29,440
That bowl must've been empty all along.

107
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:31,600
Bite Wang Anyu.

108
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:32,610
Hi.

109
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:36,800
So cute.

110
00:03:38,080 --> 00:03:38,960
Feels really nice.

111
00:03:38,960 --> 00:03:39,840
No fur, right?

112
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:40,200
No fur.

113
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:40,560
A hairless dog?

114
00:03:40,560 --> 00:03:41,280
Short-haired.

115
00:03:41,280 --> 00:03:42,120
A greyhound.

116
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:43,960
How old is it?

117
00:03:44,040 --> 00:03:44,970
A few months, maybe?

118
00:03:45,880 --> 00:03:47,480
Look, its little paws
aren't fully grown yet.

119
00:03:47,480 --> 00:03:48,050
Let's see.

120
00:03:49,240 --> 00:03:49,920
Check its teeth.

121
00:03:50,920 --> 00:03:53,040
Just a few months old.
It hasn't lost all its baby teeth.

122
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:54,280
These are still baby teeth.

123
00:03:54,280 --> 00:03:55,360
Don't get bitten.

124
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:56,040
It won't bite.

125
00:03:56,040 --> 00:03:57,320
It's got two rows of teeth now.

126
00:03:57,320 --> 00:03:59,040
This tooth should fall out soon.

127
00:03:59,040 --> 00:03:59,960
That sharp one.

128
00:03:59,960 --> 00:04:01,280
Really?

129
00:04:01,360 --> 00:04:02,790
You're Baa-Baa from now on.

130
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:11,770
I'll make a stew.

131
00:04:11,820 --> 00:04:13,060
(Still fighting over the eggplant)

132
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:14,120
Don't!

133
00:04:14,200 --> 00:04:14,880
Calm down.

134
00:04:14,880 --> 00:04:15,760
Give it to me!

135
00:04:15,760 --> 00:04:16,720
Calm down!

136
00:04:18,080 --> 00:04:19,160
I'm stewing it.

137
00:04:19,240 --> 00:04:20,800
I'm tossing it in the stew.

138
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:21,720
You do it.

139
00:04:21,720 --> 00:04:22,800
I'll help you out.

140
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:23,250
Sure.

141
00:04:23,960 --> 00:04:24,960
What are we making?

142
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:25,680
Braised eggplant?

143
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:28,260
(Gotta save the eggplant)

144
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:33,600
Can we make braised eggplant?

145
00:04:33,600 --> 00:04:34,560
Yeah, you two can.

146
00:04:34,560 --> 00:04:35,800
Alright, then we'll...

147
00:04:35,800 --> 00:04:36,700
Stew the eggplant?

148
00:04:36,700 --> 00:04:38,060
(Eggplant battle?)

149
00:04:39,780 --> 00:04:41,060
(We'll make one too)

150
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:42,280
Braised noodles with green beans.

151
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:42,880
Sure.

152
00:04:43,100 --> 00:04:45,860
(New dishes: Northeastern stew,
braised eggplant, green bean noodles)

153
00:04:45,900 --> 00:04:47,780
(A chef with nothing to cook)

154
00:04:48,160 --> 00:04:49,080
What do you wanna eat, Chengcheng?

155
00:04:49,180 --> 00:04:50,040
(I'll make it for you)

156
00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:51,080
Teng's

157
00:04:51,160 --> 00:04:52,270
back from training.

158
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:53,820
He's a chef now.

159
00:04:54,020 --> 00:04:56,460
(Chef Xu is here)

160
00:04:56,720 --> 00:04:57,600
Now...

161
00:04:57,680 --> 00:04:58,960
Can you cook now?

162
00:04:58,960 --> 00:04:59,680
I can.

163
00:04:59,680 --> 00:05:00,280
I'm telling you,

164
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:02,040
once Long Restaurant comes up,

165
00:05:02,040 --> 00:05:02,800
ask him for anything.

166
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:03,720
He can make it.

167
00:05:06,080 --> 00:05:09,080
I've got everything ready for my stew.

168
00:05:09,160 --> 00:05:10,520
Eggplant, potatoes, and peppers.

169
00:05:10,520 --> 00:05:12,020
Now you just need someone
who can cook it.

170
00:05:12,300 --> 00:05:14,420
(No clue where to start)

171
00:05:14,560 --> 00:05:17,200
I looked over and Churan
had minced that garlic

172
00:05:17,200 --> 00:05:19,020
so fine you could barely see it.

173
00:05:19,100 --> 00:05:24,780
(These hands were made
for mincing garlic)

174
00:05:24,840 --> 00:05:26,610
Am I gonna mince garlic all night?

175
00:05:27,320 --> 00:05:28,720
I think I've done five cloves already.

176
00:05:29,640 --> 00:05:30,760
Chengcheng's braised noodles

177
00:05:30,760 --> 00:05:32,320
were a big hit last season.

178
00:05:33,080 --> 00:05:34,180
Find a foolproof tutorial
for braised noodles.

179
00:05:34,180 --> 00:05:35,260
(Digital chef reviewing)

180
00:05:35,280 --> 00:05:36,600
Anyu, I've made this before.

181
00:05:36,600 --> 00:05:37,440
You make it.

182
00:05:37,440 --> 00:05:38,660
Then tell me how.

183
00:05:39,030 --> 00:05:40,860
(Forgot everything after a year)
I don't remember either.

184
00:05:40,900 --> 00:05:43,540
(Joining the review session)

185
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:44,970
Northeastern stew.

186
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:47,140
(Digital cooking coach +1)

187
00:05:48,780 --> 00:05:51,220
(Digital cooking coach +2)

188
00:05:51,680 --> 00:05:52,040
Got it.

189
00:05:52,040 --> 00:05:52,760
Okay, no problem! Let's go!

190
00:05:52,760 --> 00:05:53,760
Got it.

191
00:05:53,840 --> 00:05:54,360
That's it?

192
00:05:54,360 --> 00:05:55,080
Got it.

193
00:05:55,080 --> 00:05:56,200
One watch and I've got it.

194
00:05:56,280 --> 00:05:57,360
Seriously?

195
00:05:57,440 --> 00:05:58,080
I'm calling it now.

196
00:05:58,080 --> 00:05:59,380
(Putting it out there)

197
00:06:00,980 --> 00:06:02,660
(A true disciple of Michelin Bing)

198
00:06:07,680 --> 00:06:09,800
You need to cut off the eggplant stem.

199
00:06:09,880 --> 00:06:10,720
It's already in the pot?

200
00:06:10,720 --> 00:06:11,600
It's in there.

201
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:12,600
What? Did I see it wrong?

202
00:06:12,600 --> 00:06:13,240
No, you gotta cut it.

203
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:14,130
Cut it off.

204
00:06:15,040 --> 00:06:15,520
Cut it off?

205
00:06:15,520 --> 00:06:16,360
When you gave it to me...

206
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:17,460
I twisted it off by hand.

207
00:06:18,160 --> 00:06:19,120
You left the top on.

208
00:06:19,640 --> 00:06:20,560
I kept it.

209
00:06:20,560 --> 00:06:20,880
You kept it?

210
00:06:21,680 --> 00:06:23,600
Why? Take it out!

211
00:06:33,320 --> 00:06:34,900
Did that eggplant come alive?

212
00:06:37,100 --> 00:06:37,740
Oh my God!

213
00:06:37,800 --> 00:06:38,910
I'm staying away from you.

214
00:06:38,910 --> 00:06:39,860
(I'm out)

215
00:06:42,440 --> 00:06:43,400
That's totally normal.

216
00:06:43,400 --> 00:06:44,800
This eggplant has too much water.

217
00:06:45,020 --> 00:06:47,540
(Protective shield)

218
00:06:47,560 --> 00:06:48,500
I'll blanch these first.

219
00:06:49,180 --> 00:06:50,240
(Blanching the ribs
for the Northeastern stew)

220
00:06:50,240 --> 00:06:50,790
Bai!

221
00:06:53,520 --> 00:06:54,140
Careful.

222
00:06:54,960 --> 00:06:55,710
Careful.

223
00:06:56,120 --> 00:06:56,810
Careful.

224
00:06:57,840 --> 00:06:59,500
What are you doing?

225
00:07:01,340 --> 00:07:02,700
(The Northeastern stew begins)

226
00:07:02,720 --> 00:07:03,270
Bing!

227
00:07:04,200 --> 00:07:05,840
My oil's already in the pan.

228
00:07:05,840 --> 00:07:06,400
What next?

229
00:07:06,400 --> 00:07:07,060
Here, let me see.

230
00:07:07,060 --> 00:07:07,660
(Asking the in-person teacher)

231
00:07:08,260 --> 00:07:09,120
(Ribs go straight in)

232
00:07:09,120 --> 00:07:09,860
You didn't fry the aromatics first.

233
00:07:10,520 --> 00:07:11,960
Cook the moisture off first,
then add them.

234
00:07:11,960 --> 00:07:13,320
Add them once it's dry.

235
00:07:13,320 --> 00:07:14,520
Hu, more minced garlic.

236
00:07:15,320 --> 00:07:16,290
More garlic.

237
00:07:17,320 --> 00:07:17,960
It's yours.

238
00:07:17,960 --> 00:07:18,840
Use this.

239
00:07:18,840 --> 00:07:19,600
There's... There's

240
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:20,180
some here.

241
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:24,510
No!

242
00:07:26,760 --> 00:07:27,640
So you don't need it.

243
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:28,530
I'll take it away.

244
00:07:30,040 --> 00:07:30,720
No!

245
00:07:30,720 --> 00:07:31,000
Quick!

246
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:31,840
Scoop it out! There's still time!

247
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:33,320
No.

248
00:07:33,400 --> 00:07:34,210
Isn't that enough?

249
00:07:34,660 --> 00:07:35,520
(A chaotic kitchen)

250
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:36,920
It won't really hurt anything.

251
00:07:36,920 --> 00:07:38,680
You just added it too early.

252
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:41,120
(Chef Shen Fu's lesson)
Add garlic right before it's done.

253
00:07:41,120 --> 00:07:42,360
Or add it earlier,

254
00:07:42,360 --> 00:07:44,120
when the oil's hot.

255
00:07:44,120 --> 00:07:45,680
Just not at this point.

256
00:07:45,680 --> 00:07:46,360
Right.

257
00:07:46,360 --> 00:07:47,200
See?

258
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:48,260
Got it, Teng.

259
00:07:48,260 --> 00:07:49,460
(I'm a chef, after all)

260
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:54,760
What's in your pot?

261
00:07:54,760 --> 00:07:55,680
Ribs.

262
00:07:56,600 --> 00:07:58,000
My ribs are still here.

263
00:07:58,000 --> 00:07:58,860
Why'd you put them in there?

264
00:07:59,550 --> 00:08:00,440
To blanch them.

265
00:08:00,540 --> 00:08:02,380
(That's what the online tutorial said)

266
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:05,160
You're blanching ribs
in cold water in a clay pot?

267
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:06,480
You're blanching them in this?

268
00:08:06,900 --> 00:08:07,620
Yeah.

269
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:08,770
There were no pots left.

270
00:08:12,360 --> 00:08:13,160
Don't give her a hard time.

271
00:08:13,160 --> 00:08:14,120
She just got here.

272
00:08:14,120 --> 00:08:15,680
We could make soup.

273
00:08:15,680 --> 00:08:16,800
Make pork rib soup.

274
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:18,050
Isn't that too little meat?

275
00:08:18,440 --> 00:08:19,400
It's enough for flavor.

276
00:08:19,400 --> 00:08:20,280
Yeah, just for flavor.

277
00:08:20,280 --> 00:08:21,720
(Emergency tutorial search)

278
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:23,960
Do these really need to be blanched?

279
00:08:23,960 --> 00:08:24,600
They're already blanched.

280
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:25,920
You didn't pour out the water after?

281
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:27,020
You just added more water?

282
00:08:28,440 --> 00:08:30,440
No, let's pour it all out now.

283
00:08:30,520 --> 00:08:31,870
Okay, everyone move.

284
00:08:33,240 --> 00:08:33,680
Move!

285
00:08:33,680 --> 00:08:34,880
Quick, move!

286
